{"slug":"primitives","number":"2","title":"Primitive operations","file":"spec/ops/02-primitives.md","sections":[{"id":"2.1","number":"2.1","title":"addElement"},{"id":"2.2","number":"2.2","title":"removeElement"},{"id":"2.3","number":"2.3","title":"setProperty and unsetProperty"},{"id":"2.4","number":"2.4","title":"moveJunction"},{"id":"2.5","number":"2.5","title":"Values in primitives"}],"blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Primitives are the whole vocabulary of change: every composite (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/ops/0.1/composites","c":["chapter 4"]},"), every editor gesture and every agent request is, in the end, a sequence of these five operations and their three shorthands. Each changes the working copy in exactly one way, and each fails — failing the batch — when it cannot."]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"2.1","number":"2.1","c":["addElement"]},{"t":"code","lang":"json","v":"{ \"op\": \"addElement\", \"collection\": \"rooms\", \"id\": \"R7\", \"element\": { \"level\": \"L1\", \"anchor\": [390144, 390144], \"name\": \"Den\" } }"},{"t":"p","c":["Adds ",{"t":"code","v":"element"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"collection"}," under ",{"t":"code","v":"id"},", or under a minted ID when ",{"t":"code","v":"id"}," is absent (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/ops/0.1/transactions#1.5","c":["1.5"]},"). ",{"t":"code","v":"collection"}," is one of the eleven collections of Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.1/model#1.1","c":["1.1"]},". The element is added exactly as given; whether it is a valid element is decided when the batch is validated, after normalization."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-OPS-2.1.1","level":"MUST","c":[{"t":"code","v":"addElement"}," MUST fail with ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-OPS-005"}," when its ",{"t":"code","v":"id"}," is already used (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/ops/0.1/transactions#FS-OPS-1.5.2","c":["1.5.2"]},"), and MUST NOT otherwise check the element's content."]}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Shorthands."]}," These are ",{"t":"code","v":"addElement"}," with the collection fixed and the element's members written inline; they exist because they are the commonest edits and read naturally:"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null],"head":[["Shorthand"],["Is"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"{ \"op\": \"addJunction\", \"id\"?, \"level\", \"position\", \"join\"?, \"name\"?, \"extensions\"?, \"extras\"? }"}],[{"t":"code","v":"addElement"}," into ",{"t":"code","v":"junctions"}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"{ \"op\": \"addWall\", \"id\"?, \"level\", \"start\", \"end\", \"type\"?, \"layers\"?, \"justification\"?, \"base\"?, \"top\"?, \"name\"?, \"extensions\"?, \"extras\"? }"}],[{"t":"code","v":"addElement"}," into ",{"t":"code","v":"walls"}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"{ \"op\": \"addSeparator\", \"id\"?, \"level\", \"start\", \"end\", \"name\"?, \"extensions\"?, \"extras\"? }"}],[{"t":"code","v":"addElement"}," into ",{"t":"code","v":"separators"}]]]},{"t":"p","c":["Every operation that creates an element may carry the members every element may (",{"t":"code","v":"name"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"extensions"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"extras"},", Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.1/model#1.4","c":["1.4"]},"), and passes them into the element as given."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-OPS-2.1.2","level":"MUST","c":["A shorthand's references — ",{"t":"code","v":"level"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"start"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"end"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"position"}," — are resolved first (",{"t":"a","href":"#2.5","c":["2.5"]},"); the shorthand is then exactly the ",{"t":"code","v":"addElement"}," of the resolved values, and an applier MUST treat it so."]}," So a shorthand whose ",{"t":"code","v":"start"}," names no junction is rejected with ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-OPS-003"}," when it is resolved, where an ",{"t":"code","v":"addElement"}," with the same content is added and rejected at validation (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-002"},")."]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"2.2","number":"2.2","c":["removeElement"]},{"t":"code","lang":"json","v":"{ \"op\": \"removeElement\", \"id\": \"W12\", \"cascade\": true }"},{"t":"p","c":["Removes the element ",{"t":"code","v":"id"},". Removing an element that other elements depend on would leave them pointing at nothing, so ",{"t":"code","v":"removeElement"}," follows this table:"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null],"head":[["Removing"],["Takes with it, when ",{"t":"code","v":"cascade"}," is ",{"t":"code","v":"true"}],["Blocks, otherwise"]],"rows":[[["a building"],["its levels (and what they take)"],["its levels"]],[["a level"],["its junctions, walls, separators, rooms and slabs, and every wall's openings"],["anything on it, or any wall whose ",{"t":"code","v":"base.level"}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"top.level"}," it is"]],[["a junction"],["the walls and separators that end at it, and their openings"],["those walls and separators"]],[["a wall"],["its openings; and it is removed from any junction's ",{"t":"code","v":"join.through"},", which unsets that ",{"t":"code","v":"join"}],["its openings"]],[["a separator, room, opening or slab"],["nothing"],["nothing"]],[["a type, material or asset"],["nothing — ",{"t":"code","v":"cascade"}," does not apply"],["every element that refers to it"]]]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"code","v":"cascade"}," defaults to ",{"t":"code","v":"false"},". A wall is always removed from ",{"t":"code","v":"join.through"}," lists, because a join that names a missing wall describes nothing."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-OPS-2.2.1","level":"MUST","c":[{"t":"code","v":"removeElement"}," MUST fail with ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-OPS-003"}," when ",{"t":"code","v":"id"}," does not exist, and with ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-OPS-006"}," when the table says the removal is blocked."]}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-OPS-2.2.2","level":"MUST","c":["When ",{"t":"code","v":"cascade"}," is ",{"t":"code","v":"true"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"removeElement"}," MUST remove exactly the elements the table lists, transitively, and nothing else."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"2.3","number":"2.3","c":["setProperty and unsetProperty"]},{"t":"code","lang":"json","v":"{ \"op\": \"setProperty\", \"id\": \"W12\", \"path\": \"/justification\", \"value\": \"exteriorFace\" }\n{ \"op\": \"unsetProperty\", \"id\": \"O3\", \"path\": \"/sill\" }"},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"code","v":"setProperty"}," sets the member at ",{"t":"code","v":"path"}," — a JSON Pointer (RFC 6901), relative to the element — to ",{"t":"code","v":"value"},", creating the member, and any missing objects on the way to it, if needed; an array element is addressed by its index. ",{"t":"code","v":"unsetProperty"}," removes the member, so that its default applies again. ",{"t":"code","v":"id"}," is an element reference, or one of three reserved targets: ",{"t":"code","v":"$project"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"$site"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"$document"},". ",{"t":"code","v":"$document"}," addresses the document's top-level members other than its collections: ",{"t":"code","v":"floorspec"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"project"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"site"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"extensionsUsed"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"extensionsRequired"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"extensions"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"extras"}," — so ",{"t":"code","v":"unsetProperty"}," of ",{"t":"code","v":"$document"}," ",{"t":"code","v":"/site"}," removes the site. Setting a member of ",{"t":"code","v":"$site"}," creates the site if the project has none."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-OPS-2.3.1","level":"MUST","c":[{"t":"code","v":"setProperty"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"unsetProperty"}," MUST fail with ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-OPS-003"}," when ",{"t":"code","v":"id"}," does not exist, when ",{"t":"code","v":"path"}," is empty or is not a JSON Pointer, when it leads through a value that is neither an object nor an array or to an array index that does not exist, or when it names a member of ",{"t":"code","v":"$document"}," that the list above does not, and ",{"t":"code","v":"unsetProperty"}," MUST also fail with ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-OPS-003"}," when the member does not exist."]}]},{"t":"p","c":["A ",{"t":"code","v":"path"}," cannot change an element's ID or move it between collections: there is no member for either. Changing an ID is not an edit Floorspec has."]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"2.4","number":"2.4","c":["moveJunction"]},{"t":"code","lang":"json","v":"{ \"op\": \"moveJunction\", \"id\": \"J4\", \"to\": [780288, 0] }"},{"t":"p","c":["Sets the junction's ",{"t":"code","v":"position"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"to"},". It is ",{"t":"code","v":"setProperty"}," of ",{"t":"code","v":"/position"},", named, because moving a junction is what moving walls, resizing rooms and dragging corners all come down to."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-OPS-2.4.1","level":"MUST","c":["An applier MUST treat ",{"t":"code","v":"moveJunction"}," exactly as ",{"t":"code","v":"setProperty"}," of the junction's ",{"t":"code","v":"/position"},"."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"2.5","number":"2.5","c":["Values in primitives"]},{"t":"p","c":["Primitives carry resolved values: lengths are integers and points are ",{"t":"code","v":"[x, y]"}," — except that a primitive in a batch may use the reference grammar of ",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/ops/0.1/references","c":["chapter 3"]}," in a member its definition types as a length, point or element reference (",{"t":"code","v":"removeElement"},"'s ",{"t":"code","v":"id"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"moveJunction"},"'s ",{"t":"code","v":"to"},", a shorthand's ",{"t":"code","v":"level"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"start"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"end"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"position"},"), and is resolved first like any composite; never inside ",{"t":"code","v":"element"}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"value"},", which are taken as given. The ",{"t":"code","v":"resolved"}," echo (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/ops/0.1/transactions#1.4","c":["1.4"]},") always contains the integers."]}]}
